# Checking an age threshold
#
# A person's birth date is compared with the current local time. A backward
# rule uses date arithmetic to test whether the person is older than a
# specified duration.

@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix time: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/time#> .
@prefix math: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/math#> .
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .
@prefix : <https://example.org/#> .

# A person and their date of birth.
:patH :birthDay "1944-08-21"^^xsd:date .

# A backward rule: S's age is above A when the time between S's birth date
# and the current local time is longer than the duration A. Because the rule
# reads the clock, its answer can change from one run to the next.
{
    ?S :ageAbove ?A
} <= {
    ?S :birthDay ?B .
    "" time:localTime ?D .
    (?D ?B) math:difference ?F .
    ?F math:greaterThan ?A .
} .

# Ask whether :patH is older than 80 years, and record the answer.
{
    ?S :ageAbove "P80Y"^^xsd:duration .
} => {
    :test :is true .
} .
